<title>USA: Sparks pegs Brazil soy crop at 26.5 mln T - trade.</title>
<headline>Sparks pegs Brazil soy crop at 26.5 mln T - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. grain traders said Spark's Companies has estimated the Brazil soybean crop at 26.5 million tonnes, unchanged from the latest U.S. Agriculture Department estimate released February 12.</p>
<p>Sparks Companies officials declined to comment.</p>
<p>Sparks also estimated the Argentina corn crop at 14.9 million tonnes up from USDA's February estimate of 14.5 million. It estimated Argentina's wheat crop at 15.6 million tonnes up from USDA's estimate of 15.5 million.  </p>
<p>Traders said Sparks also estimated the Argentina soybean crop at 13.9 million tonnes, slightly above USDA's February estimate of 13.5 million.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
